+> **Description:** Qdrant’s README describes a high-performance, large-scale vector database and search engine for the next generation of AI applications. In practice, it is the retrieval layer behind many serious document-assistant deployments, especially when semantic search quality and filtering matter. Insurance teams can use it to power policy clause retrieval, endorsement lookup, prospect research, and historical account intelligence across structured and unstructured content. The project is Apache-2.0 licensed, Rust-based, and highly active, making it a strong infrastructure choice when a simple all-in-one tool is no longer enough.
+
