+## TL;DR
+- `RAGFlow`, `AnythingLLM`, and `Flowise` are the fastest ways to stand up private knowledge assistants for policy, underwriting, renewal, and claims documents.
+- `Docling`, `Unstructured`, `PaddleOCR`, `OCRmyPDF`, and `Paperless-ngx` cover the document ingestion layer insurance agencies usually need before any LLM workflow works reliably.
+- `Whisper`, `faster-whisper`, `Pipecat`, and `LiveKit Agents` are the strongest open-source options for call notes, meeting summaries, and voice-driven agent workflows.
+- `Chatwoot`, `Twenty`, `Activepieces`, `Documenso`, and `NocoDB` fill the operational gap around customer communication, CRM, signatures, and workflow automation.
+
+## Why This List
+Insurance agencies deal with dense PDFs, renewal packets, ACORD-style forms, email-heavy servicing, call notes, policy comparisons, and regulated internal knowledge. That makes open-source AI especially attractive: the best AI tools for insurance agents are often the ones you can self-host, inspect, and wire into your own data retention and compliance model.
