+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open-source AI tools for insurance agents in 2026?
+For most agencies, the strongest starting stack is `AnythingLLM` or `RAGFlow` for private knowledge chat, `Docling` or `Unstructured` for document ingestion, `Whisper` or `faster-whisper` for call transcription, and `Activepieces` or `Chatwoot` for operational workflow glue.
+
+### Which open-source AI tools help insurance agents work with policy PDFs and scanned forms?
+`Docling`, `Unstructured`, `Marker`, `OCRmyPDF`, `PaddleOCR`, `Tesseract`, and `Paperless-ngx` are the clearest GitHub-native options here. They cover OCR, parsing, indexing, document management, and conversion into structured formats that LLM systems can actually use.
+
+### Is there an open-source CRM with AI potential for insurance agencies?
+Yes. `Twenty` is the strongest CRM-specific fit in this list, while `NocoDB` can act as a lighter operational database for agencies that want flexible workflows first. Both can be paired with retrieval, summarization, and automation tools from the rest of the stack.
+
+### What is the best self-hosted AI assistant for an insurance agency knowledge base?
+`AnythingLLM`, `RAGFlow`, `LibreChat`, `Flowise`, and `FastGPT` are the strongest starting points. The right choice depends on whether the team wants a quick workspace-style deployment, a visual workflow builder, or a more retrieval-focused engine with stronger control over context and citations.
+
+### Are there many GitHub repositories built specifically for insurance agents?
+No. That is the main research constraint behind this repository. Direct insurance-agent AI repos are still sparse, so this list focuses on the real open-source building blocks agencies can combine into an insurance-specific stack instead of pretending the niche is deeper than it is.
+
+### Which open-source repos are best for insurance call notes and customer service transcripts?
+`Whisper`, `faster-whisper`, and `whisper.cpp` are the core transcription options. If you need interactive voice systems instead of just transcripts, shortlist `Pipecat` and `LiveKit Agents`.
+
